# SABOTAGE: T79 (spec §I6 macros composer palette + CSAT loop closed) — the
# fail-honest CSAT send guarantee (ADR-014 Invariant D1, mirrored onto
# `Samen.Scopes.Support.CsatSurvey.send_survey/3`): `sent_at` must be set IFF the
# delivery chokepoint genuinely returned `{:ok, _}`. This sabotage calls
# `mark_sent/1` in the `:adapter_unconfigured` (BLOCKED) branch too — the exact
# lie ADR-014 forbids: a survey that was NEVER actually dispatched (no delivery
# adapter configured) would be recorded as sent, so an operator inspecting the
# token table could not distinguish a genuinely-delivered survey from one that
# silently never left the chokepoint.
